International College At American International College (AIC) , we believe in the power of education to transform lives. Located in the heart of Springfield, Massachusetts, our vibrant campus blends historic charm with modern innovation. With approximately 2,000 undergraduate and graduate students, AIC offers a close-knit, supportive culture where your work makes a meaningful impact. Our mission is to provide access to a holistic education in an inclusive environment that propels a diverse community of learners to personal growth and professional success. Guided by this purpose, we cultivate a campus where students, faculty, and staff feel a true sense of belonging, benefit from innovative education, and participate in experiences that empower them to thrive in their careers and communities. Whether you're teaching, advising, or supporting operations, you'll be part of a collaborative team that values purpose-driven education, personal growth, and professional achievement. We are deeply committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion, and we actively seek candidates who bring unique perspectives and experiences to our campus. Make a difference where it counts. At AIC, every position plays a part in empowering students and strengthening the AIC experience. American International College is an equal opportunity employer . We are committed to building and sustaining an inclusive and equitable working and learning environments for all. We welcome applicants of all backgrounds and do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected characteristic as defined by law. About the Role: The Adjunct Faculty in Physical Therapy plays a critical role in educating and mentoring students pursuing careers in physical therapy. This position involves delivering high-quality instruction that integrates theoretical knowledge with practical application, preparing students to excel in clinical environments. The faculty member will contribute to curriculum development, ensuring that course content remains current with advancements in physical therapy practices and research. Additionally, the role requires fostering a supportive and engaging learning environment that encourages critical thinking and professional growth. Ultimately, the adjunct faculty member helps shape the next generation of physical therapy professionals by providing expert guidance and promoting evidence-based practice. Minimum Qualifications: A minimum of a Doctor of Physical Therapy (DPT) degree from an accredited institution. Current and unrestricted physical therapy license in the United StatesPractice should. Demonstrated experience in clinical physical therapy practice. Prior teaching or instructional experience in physical therapy or related health sciences. Strong communication skills and the ability to engage students in a virtual or in-person classroom setting. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with curriculum development and academic program assessment. Advanced certifications or specializations in physical therapy (e.g., Orthopedics, Neurology). Experience with online teaching platforms and educational technolog, preferably in the neurology specialties. Research experience or scholarly publications in physical therapy or rehabilitation sciences. Membership in professional organizations such as the American Physical Therapy Association (APTA). Responsibilities: Deliver lectures and laboratory sessions in physical therapy courses according to the academic schedule. Develop and update course materials, including syllabi, assignments, and assessments, to reflect current best practices and research. Provide academic advising and mentorship to students, supporting their professional development and clinical readiness. Evaluate student performance through grading assignments, exams, and practical demonstrations, offering constructive feedback. Collaborate with full-time faculty and participate in departmental meetings to contribute to program improvement and accreditation processes. Skills: The required skills enable the adjunct faculty member to effectively convey complex physical therapy concepts and clinical techniques to students, ensuring comprehension and practical application. Strong communication and interpersonal skills facilitate meaningful interactions with students, fostering an inclusive and motivating learning environment. Organizational skills are essential for managing course materials, grading, and coordinating with other faculty members. Preferred skills such as curriculum development and familiarity with educational technology enhance the ability to innovate teaching methods and adapt to diverse learning modalities. Research and professional engagement skills support the integration of current evidence-based practices into the curriculum, enriching the educational experience. AIC is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Apply Now Related Searches: Physical Therapy Want to learn more about working for this employer? View Profile Advertisement Create your free job search account Edit and manage Job Alerts Post your resume/CV Track your applications Join Now Have an account? Sign in To Apply for this Job Please be sure to read the job posting carefully and submit all required information. Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information © 2026 HigherEdJobs. U.S. Patent 8,548,928 Email this job to a friend Email Job To Please enter a single email address Your Em