 engaging Adjunct Faculty member to teach courses in our Bachelor of Science in Fire Science and Emergency Services program in a fully online environment. This part-time role is essential in helping students develop the knowledge, leadership skills, and professional competencies needed for careers in fire protection, emergency services, emergency management, and public safety. The faculty member will be part of a supportive academic environment and will collaborate with colleagues for guidance and support related to curriculum, course expectations, and instructional best practices, ensuring consistency and quality across course sections. Minimum Qualifications: - Master's degree in Fire Science, Fire Protection Administration, Emergency Management, Public Safety Administration, Homeland Security, Occupational Safety, or a closely related field from an accredited institution - Professional experience in fire service, emergency services, emergency management, public safety, or a related field - Demonstrated ability to teach or train adult learners in professional, academic, or workforce settings - Strong written and verbal communication skills - Commitment to student success and inclusive teaching practices Preferred Qualifications: - Prior experience teaching college-level Fire Science or Emergency Services courses, particularly in an online environment - Experience working with diverse and/or non-traditional student populations - Current or former leadership experience within fire, EMS, emergency management, or public safety organizations - Relevant professional certifications (e.g., Fire Officer, Executive Fire Officer, Certified Emergency Manager, FEMA/ICS/NIMS credentials) - Experience using learning management systems and online instructional technologies Responsibilities: - Teach undergraduate Fire Science and Emergency Services courses in an online, asynchronous format - Deliver engaging online instruction that promotes critical thinking, problem-solving, and professional application of course concepts - Assess student work and provide timely, constructive feedback - Maintain accurate course records, including attendance, participation, and grades - Be available for student support through virtual office hours, email, and scheduled meetings - Adhere to institutional policies, procedures, and academic standards - Collaborate with departmental faculty and leadership to support student success and program quality Skills: - Strong instructional and online classroom facilitation skills - Ability to clearly communicate complex fire science, emergency management, and public safety concepts - Effective time management and organizational skills - Collaborative mindset and willingness to engage with faculty colleagues - Commitment to fostering an inclusive and supportive learning environment - Adaptability and responsiveness to student needs - Proficiency with online learning platforms and educational technology - Ability to connect academic concepts with real-world fire service and emergency management practices AIC is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Apply Now Related Searches: Fire Science Want to learn more about working for this employer? View Profile Advertisement Create your free job search account Edit and manage Job Alerts Post your resume/CV Track your applications Join Now Have an account? Sign in To Apply for this Job Please be sure to read the job posting carefully and submit all required information. Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Job Seekers Search Jobs Job Seeker Login Advice & News Newsletter Sign-Up Employers Post A Job All Recruitment Products Employer Login Testimonials Company About Us Contact Us Advertise with Us Our Audience Privacy Policy | Terms of Use | Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information © 2026 HigherEdJobs. U.S. Patent 8,54